{
  "$comment": [
    "Guard for the CHECK-constraint-vs-code-drift bug class.",
    "",
    "drizzle/migrations/0050_data_validation_checks.sql pinned text vocabularies as",
    "CHECK constraints. Code kept growing and the constraints did not, so writes",
    "started failing with 23514 — SILENTLY where the caller swallows the error",
    "(createNotification returns false, logActivity caught to console.warn) and",
    "LOUDLY where a route propagates it. Three live examples this file now covers:",
    "chk_notifications_type (4 allowed vs 20 written: the notifications table held",
    "zero rows for its entire history while cron reported notified:4),",
    "chk_ai_activity_action (6 allowed vs 5 more written: ai_activity also held zero",
    "rows), and chk_announcements_type (a user-visible 500).",
    "",
    "required — every value must exist in the DB CHECK. A missing value is the bug:",
    "  the write is rejected, and 3 of 4 call sites so far swallowed it.",
    "legacy   — the DB allows it and no current writer produces it. Rows may already",
    "  carry it, so it must never be removed from the constraint without a data check.",
    "declaredIn — files that must literally contain each required value, so this",
    "  registry cannot drift from the code it claims to describe.",
    "",
    "Anything the DB allows that appears in neither list is reported as a warning,",
    "not a failure: vocabulary creep is normal, undocumented creep is not."
  ],
  "constraints": [
    {
      "id": "notifications.type",
      "constraint": "chk_notifications_type",
      "table": "notifications",
      "column": "type",
      "migration": "0101_notifications_type_allows_app_vocabulary",
      "declaredIn": ["lib/notifications.ts"],
      "required": [
        "info",
        "task_assigned",
        "task_due",
        "task_overdue",
        "deal_stage",
        "deal_assigned",
        "deal_won",
        "contact_assigned",
        "mention",
        "invite_accepted",
        "team_joined",
        "limit_warning",
        "trial_expiring",
        "lead_warming",
        "sla_breach",
        "sla_escalation",
        "contract_renewal",
        "subscription_renewal",
        "ai_followup_sent",
        "system"
      ],
      "legacy": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ai_activity.action",
      "constraint": "chk_ai_activity_action",
      "table": "ai_activity",
      "column": "action",
      "migration": "0102_ai_activity_action_allows_app_vocabulary",
      "declaredIn": [],
      "required": [
        "draft",
        "lead_scoring",
        "predict_deal",
        "suggest_followup",
        "insights",
        "email_draft",
        "auto_followup",
        "score_lead",
        "sentiment_analysis"
      ],
      "legacy": ["enrich_contact", "summarize"],
      "writers": {
        "draft": ["app/api/tenant/ai/route.ts"],
        "lead_scoring": ["app/api/tenant/ai/route.ts"],
        "predict_deal": ["app/api/tenant/ai/route.ts"],
        "suggest_followup": ["app/api/tenant/ai/route.ts"],
        "insights": ["app/api/tenant/ai/insights/route.ts"],
        "email_draft": ["app/api/tenant/ai/email-draft/route.ts"],
        "auto_followup": ["lib/ai/auto-followup.ts"],
        "score_lead": ["lib/ai/scoring.ts"],
        "sentiment_analysis": ["lib/ai/sentiment.ts"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "scheduled_reports.type",
      "constraint": "chk_scheduled_reports_type",
      "table": "scheduled_reports",
      "column": "type",
      "migration": "0103_scheduled_reports_type_allows_exported_entities",
      "declaredIn": [],
      "required": ["deals", "tasks", "companies"],
      "legacy": ["pipeline", "revenue", "contacts", "performance"],
      "writers": {
        "deals": ["app/api/cron/scheduled-report-delivery/route.ts"],
        "tasks": ["app/api/cron/scheduled-report-delivery/route.ts"],
        "companies": ["app/api/cron/scheduled-report-delivery/route.ts"]
      },
      "note": [
        "'leads' and 'summary' are deliberately NOT added. They are accepted by the",
        "free-text create route (app/api/tenant/reports/scheduled/route.ts validates",
        "type as z.string().max(50)) and exportEntityFor() silently maps them onto the",
        "contacts export — so a 'leads' report emails a contacts CSV. Adding them would",
        "bless that. The default branch now throws instead; whether to support them",
        "properly is a separate decision."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "integrations.type",
      "constraint": "chk_integrations_type",
      "table": "integrations",
      "column": "type",
      "migration": "0104_integrations_type_allows_configured_providers",
      "declaredIn": [],
      "required": [
        "google",
        "outlook",
        "slack",
        "webhook",
        "sms",
        "mailgun",
        "openai",
        "sendgrid"
      ],
      "legacy": ["zoom"],
      "writers": {
        "google": ["lib/calendar-sync/google.ts"],
        "outlook": ["lib/calendar-sync/outlook.ts"],
        "slack": ["lib/integrations/providers/slack.ts"],
        "webhook": ["app/api/tenant/webhooks/route.ts"],
        "sms": ["lib/automation/engine.ts"],
        "mailgun": ["lib/integrations/providers/mailgun.ts"],
        "openai": ["lib/integrations/providers/openai.ts"],
        "sendgrid": ["lib/integrations/providers/sendgrid.ts"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sequence_steps.step_type",
      "constraint": "chk_sequence_steps_step_type",
      "table": "sequence_steps",
      "column": "step_type",
      "migration": null,
      "declaredIn": [],
      "required": ["email", "task", "delay"],
      "legacy": ["whatsapp"],
      "writers": {
        "email": ["lib/api/schemas.ts"],
        "task": ["lib/api/schemas.ts"],
        "delay": ["lib/api/schemas.ts"]
      },
      "note": [
        "No migration: the DB was always right. The bug was in code — the zod schema",
        "and the builder offered 'wait', which the constraint never allowed, so every",
        "sequence with a wait step failed on insert. Fixed in lib/api/schemas.ts,",
        "lib/api/schemas/automation.ts and components/tenant/sequence-builder.tsx.",
        "'call' and 'ab_test' are still offered by the builder UI and still rejected",
        "by zod — reported, not fixed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "announcements.type",
      "constraint": "chk_announcements_type",
      "table": "announcements",
      "column": "type",
      "migration": null,
      "declaredIn": ["lib/api/schemas/superadmin.ts"],
      "required": ["info", "warning", "update", "feature"],
      "legacy": [],
      "writers": {},
      "note": [
        "Regression guard for #35: the UI and zod offered a type the constraint",
        "rejected, which surfaced as a 500 rather than silence."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
